ble range for diabetic patient", "Primary neurological syndrome: neurological deficits are nonfocal and mild", "Vasovagal syncope: no syncope reported to anchor this mechanism", "Other systemic inflammatory disorders: insufficient evidence of localized infection or organ-specific inflammation"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (weight loss, fever, night sweats)", "Pancytopenia with leukemic blasts", "Unexplained visual acuity decline and ataxia"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.8583027522935779, "posterior": 0.23884716336884113, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Chronic MPN in accelerated phase typically has <20% blasts in peripheral blood; 35% blasts strongly favor myeloid neoplasm (B1) over this entity (B3)."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.85, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.390137614678899, "posterior": 0.40085585960636777, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["High blast percentage supports myeloid neoplasm (B1) over chronic MPN (B3), but the 35% blast count is slightly lower than typical for de novo ALL (B2) and lac…"], "evidence_against": ["The 35% blast count is below the typical 80-90% seen in de novo ALL, but pancytopenia is consistent with ALL. Lack of lymphoid features (e.g., lymphadenopathy)…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reaso