ood and pancytopenia (Hb 10g/dL, platelets 109k) in this 57-year-old with constitutional symptoms strongly support myeloid neoplasm over lymphoid or chronic MPN?", "summary": "High blast percentage supports myeloid neoplasm (B1) over chronic MPN (B3), but the 35% blast count is slightly lower than typical for de novo ALL (B2) and lacks lymphoid features."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the 35% blasts in peripheral blood and pancytopenia in this 57-year-old align with de novo ALL, which typically presents with higher blast counts and more pronounced lymphoid features?", "summary": "The 35% blast count is below the typical 80-90% seen in de novo ALL, but pancytopenia is consistent with ALL. Lack of lymphoid features (e.g., lymphadenopathy) weakens this alignment."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of 35% blasts and pancytopenia in this 57-year-old with constitutional symptoms strongly favor a myeloid neoplasm over chronic myeloproliferative disorders in accelerated phase?", "summary": "Chronic MPN in accelerated phase typically has <20% blasts in peripheral blood; 35% blasts strongly favor myeloid neoplasm (B1) over this entity (B3)."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the normal serum creatinine (1.1 mg/dL) and absence of splenomegaly in this 57-year-old contradict Richter's transformation (CLL→ALL) as the cause of blasts, which would require a pre-existing C…", "summary": "The absence of CLL history and normal renal function (contrary to Richter's typical renal involvement) argues against Richter's transformation (B4), though this remains a weak effect."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute onset (days) of constitutional symptoms and absence of organ involvement in this 57-year-old argue against chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms (e.g., CML, PV) in accelerated phase,…", "summary": "Subacute presentation argues against chronic MPN in accelerated phase (B