vated white blood cell count'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B2", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.513}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "posterior": 0.401, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 1, "disconfirming": 1, "last_disconfirming_digest": "The 35% blast count is below the typical 80-90% seen in de novo ALL, but pancytopenia is consistent with ALL. Lack of l…"}, "action_intents": [{"t": 4, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B3", "B1"]}}, "parent_branch": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "posterior": 0.23884716336884113, "danger": 0.9, "evidence_for": ["High blast percentage supports myeloid neoplasm (B1) over chronic MPN (B3), but the 35% blast count is slightly lower than typical for de novo ALL (B2) and lacks lymphoid features.", "Chronic MPN in accelerated phase typically has <20% blasts in peripheral blood; 35% blasts strongly favor myeloid neoplasm (B1) over this entity (B3)."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of chronic disease progression leading to blasts?", "Presence of marrow fibrosis or extramedullary disease?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Bone marrow biopsy for lineage determination", "Cytogenetics including BCR-ABL1 testing"]}, "target_level": 2}
